Subject: [PATCH] g_iphone: switch roles only after the host took our ACK, and come back after a failed switch
Upstream-Status: Pending

Two findings from a NAC Wave 2 (Continental, Toyota Proace Verso) capture
with the dwc2 instrumentation of kernel patch 0022, catplay-firmware
issue #1:

  [1.963945] iPhone: setup bmReq=0x40 bReq=0x51 wValue=0x0001 ...
  [1.964306] dwc2 13500000.usb: drd role_sw_set: requested role=1 phy_mode=1
  [1.964486] iPhone: status -> disabled
  [2.165839] dwc2 13500000.usb: hprt0 sample 1/24: HPRT0=00001000 [PWR ] lnsts=0
  ...
  [8.048451] dwc2 13500000.usb: hprt0 sample 24/24: HPRT0=00001000 [PWR ] lnsts=0
  [7.136484] iPhone: role-switch accessory probe failed: -19
  [9.184436] iPhone: rebinding gadget after role-switch failure debounce
  [9.184470] iPhone: status -> initial
  (nothing further on USB, ever)

1. We drop the device role 360us after the 0x51 SETUP packet.

   0x51 has no data stage; the head unit learns that we accepted it only
   when it collects the zero-length status packet. f_iphone_setup() set
   the RoleSwitch status - which schedules the host transition - before
   even queueing that ZLP, and the work ran 360us later. The vendor
   firmware forces host mode 18ms after the same request:

     [3.328934] f_audio_setup crtl_request : bRequestType:0x40 bRequest:0x51
     [3.346795] ---Forced switching Host mode!
     [3.647644] usb usb1-port1: hub_port_connect:4838 portchange=0 portstatus=257
     [3.797855] usb 1-1: new high-speed USB device number 2 using dwc2

   and its head unit shows up as a device 300ms later. Ours never does:
   CONNSTS stays 0 for the full six seconds our port is powered, so the
   head unit either never got our ACK or gave up on the transfer when the
   bus dropped underneath it.

   Whether that is really what happens is not proven, so this patch makes
   it measurable as well as fixing it: the RoleSwitch transition is moved
   into the completion callback of the status-stage ZLP, and the callback
   logs how long the host took to collect it and whether it succeeded:

     iPhone: role switch acknowledged by host after <N>us

   A capture without that line, or with a negative status in it, says the
   ACK never made it out. On top of that the 20ms settle time the original
   author had in role_switch_work (commented out, was 70ms) is restored,
   which puts our sequence in the same place as the vendor's.

2. After a failed switch the dongle stays in host mode for good.

   role_switch_work goes to host with manage_gadget_lifecycle=false, so the
   composite driver stays registered. The rebind work then calls
   iphone_dev_bind_gadget(), which returned early on driver_registered
   before ever setting the role back to device. Result: the controller
   keeps its port powered in host mode, the head unit sees nothing on the
   bus, and neither side can retry until the dongle is unplugged. Every
   capture we have ends this way.

   The role is now set to device before the driver_registered check. For
   every other caller that is a cached no-op. This also gives the next
   capture a discriminator: if the head unit re-enumerates us the moment
   we are back in device mode, it never left host mode itself.

Written against catplay-labs/catplay master with 0001 applied. Compiled
and run on hardware: not yet.
---
 f_iphone.c   | 62 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 iphone_dev.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/f_iphone.c
+++ b/f_iphone.c
@@ -3,6 +3,9 @@
 #include "interfaces.h"
 #include "hid.h"
 
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
+#include <linux/math64.h>
+
 #define IPHONE_REQ_USBOOT 0x88
 #define IPHONE_REQ_GADGET 0x99
 
@@ -150,6 +153,54 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * Role switch (vendor request 0x51) handshake.
+ *
+ * 0x51 is a two-stage control transfer: SETUP, then a status-stage IN that
+ * our zero-length packet answers. Only once the head unit has collected that
+ * ZLP does it know we agreed to swap roles. Tearing the device role down
+ * before then leaves the head unit with a control transfer that ended in a
+ * disconnect, and no reason to become a device itself.
+ *
+ * g_iphone_set_status(RoleSwitch) schedules the host transition, and on a
+ * NAC Wave 2 dmesg shows it taking effect 360us after the SETUP packet,
+ * where the vendor firmware takes 18ms. So the transition is now armed from
+ * the ZLP's completion callback, which is exactly the moment the host has
+ * acknowledged us, and the time it took is logged so a capture shows
+ * whether the ACK made it out at all.
+ *
+ * There is one composite ep0 request and one gadget, so the pending state
+ * is kept in file scope. If the host never runs the status stage and never
+ * sends another SETUP either, the callback never fires and the role switch
+ * does not happen - a head unit that does that would not have switched
+ * roles anyway.
+ */
+static struct g_iphone *role_switch_ack_gadget;
+static void (*role_switch_ack_orig_complete)(struct usb_ep *ep,
+					     struct usb_request *req);
+static u64 role_switch_ack_queued_ns;
+
+static void f_iphone_role_switch_ack_complete(struct usb_ep *ep,
+					      struct usb_request *req)
+{
+	struct g_iphone *iphone_gadget = role_switch_ack_gadget;
+	u64 dt_us = div_u64(ktime_get_ns() - role_switch_ack_queued_ns, 1000);
+
+	req->complete = role_switch_ack_orig_complete;
+	if (role_switch_ack_orig_complete)
+		role_switch_ack_orig_complete(ep, req);
+
+	if (req->status)
+		pr_warn("iPhone: role switch status stage ended with %d after %lluus - switching anyway\n",
+			req->status, dt_us);
+	else
+		pr_info("iPhone: role switch acknowledged by host after %lluus\n",
+			dt_us);
+
+	if (iphone_gadget)
+		g_iphone_set_status(iphone_gadget, RoleSwitch);
+}
+
+/*
  * Accept a host-to-device data stage on ep0 and discard it. The direction of
  * the transfer is taken from the SETUP packet by the UDC, so queueing a
  * request of wLength bytes receives them and completes the status stage.
@@ -225,14 +276,29 @@
 			return ep0_zlp(cdev);
 		}
 		case 0x51: /* Role Switch */
+		{
+			int ret;
+
 			pr_info("iPhone: Role Switch requested");
 			if (!cdev->req || !cdev->gadget->ep0)
 				return -ENODEV;
 
 			iphone_gadget->role_switch_requested = true;
-			g_iphone_set_status(iphone_gadget, RoleSwitch);
 
-			return ep0_zlp(cdev);
+			/* The status transition happens once the host has our ZLP. */
+			role_switch_ack_gadget = iphone_gadget;
+			role_switch_ack_orig_complete = cdev->req->complete;
+			role_switch_ack_queued_ns = ktime_get_ns();
+			cdev->req->complete = f_iphone_role_switch_ack_complete;
+
+			ret = ep0_zlp(cdev);
+			if (ret) {
+				cdev->req->complete = role_switch_ack_orig_complete;
+				iphone_gadget->role_switch_requested = false;
+				pr_warn("iPhone: role switch ZLP queue failed: %d\n", ret);
+			}
+			return ret;
+		}
 
 		case 0x53: /* Capabilities */
 		{
--- a/iphone_dev.c
+++ b/iphone_dev.c
@@ -13,7 +13,12 @@
 #include "iap2_scan.h"
 
 #define IPHONE_ROLE_SWITCH_REBIND_DEBOUNCE_MS 1000
-#define IPHONE_ROLE_SWITCH_HOST_DELAY_MS 70
+/*
+ * Settle time between the head unit acknowledging 0x51 and us dropping the
+ * device role. The vendor firmware forces host mode 18ms after the request
+ * on a NAC Wave 2; this is the same order of magnitude.
+ */
+#define IPHONE_ROLE_SWITCH_HOST_DELAY_MS 20
 #define IPHONE_RECOVERY_COMMAND "/usr/bin/carlinkit_otalib usboot"
 #define IPHONE_RECOVERY_COMMAND_GADGET "/usr/bin/carlinkit_otalib gadget"
 
@@ -156,15 +161,22 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	if (data->driver_registered)
-		return 0;
-
-	/* Before bind, always enter USB_ROLE_DEVICE */
+	/*
+	 * Before bind, always enter USB_ROLE_DEVICE. This must come before the
+	 * driver_registered check: the role-switch path goes to host without
+	 * unregistering the driver, so after a failed switch the driver is
+	 * still registered while the controller sits in host mode. Returning
+	 * early here left the dongle in host mode for good, with nothing on
+	 * the bus for the head unit to enumerate or retry against.
+	 */
 	ret = iphone_dev_set_otg_role_internal(data, USB_ROLE_DEVICE, false);
 	if (ret) {
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	if (data->driver_registered)
+		return 0;
+
 	pr_info("iPhone: registering gadget\n");
 	ret = c2a_usb_composite_probe(&data->driver->drv);
 	if (ret) {
@@ -437,7 +449,7 @@
 		data->role_switch_rebind_scheduled = false;
 	}
 
-	// msleep(IPHONE_ROLE_SWITCH_HOST_DELAY_MS);
+	msleep(IPHONE_ROLE_SWITCH_HOST_DELAY_MS);
 
 	if (iphone_dev_set_otg_role_internal(data, USB_ROLE_HOST, false)) {
 	// if (iphone_dev_set_otg_role(&data->g, USB_ROLE_HOST)) {
